Subject: pdsched: call the iOS shell once per frame, before inputUpdate()

The iOS shell (app/ios/) has work that must happen on the game's own thread at
a known point in the frame and nowhere else: draining the :8775 console
bridge's command queue, publishing the injected touch/pad state, consuming a
queued perfectdark:// deep link, and reading the frame counters the pacing
instrument reports (docs/pacing.md).

Before inputUpdate() is the one correct place. Anything the shell injects -
the floating stick, the drag-look degrees, a bridge `pad` press - is then read
by THIS frame's inputReadController() rather than the next one, so a bridge
command and its effect are never a frame apart, which is what makes
scripts/sim-validate.sh's assertions deterministic.

One function, one call, behind PLATFORM_IOS: on every other platform this file
is byte for byte upstream's.

diff --git a/port/src/pdsched.c b/port/src/pdsched.c
index fe47662cb..da6d3f44d 100644
--- a/port/src/pdsched.c
+++ b/port/src/pdsched.c
@@ -247,6 +247,11 @@ void schedSubmitTask(OSSched *sc, OSScTask *t)
 	}
 }
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+// app/ios/PDShell.m — the iOS shell's per-frame entry point.
+extern void pdIosFrameHook(void);
+#endif
+
 void schedStartFrame(OSSched *sc)
 {
 	videoStartFrame();
@@ -282,6 +287,16 @@ void schedEndFrame(OSSched *sc)
 {
 	sc->frameCount++;
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+	// The iOS shell's one call into the frame, on the game's own thread and at
+	// a known point: before inputUpdate(), so anything it injects (the touch
+	// layer's stick and look, a pad button, a :8775 bridge command) is read by
+	// this frame rather than the next. Everything the shell does to the engine
+	// happens here; nothing else in the app touches engine state off-thread.
+	// app/ios/PDShell.m.
+	pdIosFrameHook();
+#endif
+
 #if PAL
 	if (!g_Resetting && (sc->frameCount & 1)) {
